    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipTier` feature as a **derived, read-only** attribute, following the existing precedent in this codebase (`getMembershipNumber()`, `getDisplayName()`, `getInitials()` are all `@Transient` getters derived from an owner's own fields).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/MembershipTier.java`** (new) \u2014 a small enum with the two tiers `SILVER` and `BRONZE`, giving the concept a type-safe home rather than passing raw strings around.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getMembershipTier()` deriving the tier from the owner's own state:\n   ```java\n   boolean noNamesakes = this.namesakeCount != null && this.namesakeCount == 0;\n   boolean hasEmail = this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank();\n   return noNamesakes && hasEmail ? MembershipTier.SILVER : MembershipTier.BRONZE;\n   ```\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `membershipTier` on the `Owner` schema as a read-only string enum (`SILVER`/`BRONZE`). The DTO is generated from this spec, and MapStruct maps the model enum \u2192 DTO enum automatically by name, so no mapper changes were needed.\n\nThe logic lives with the other derived owner attributes (single responsibility, no new catch-all), and both new tests plus the full suite pass.",
